{"id":"dalton-highway","title":"Dalton Highway to Prudhoe Bay","who":"Classic route · Alaska's Haul Road by motorcycle","when":"June to August","vehicle":"Adventure motorcycle, 4–6 days return","kind":"moto","color":"#475569","summary":"The 414-mile road built to supply the Alaska pipeline, from the boreal forest across the Arctic Circle and the Brooks Range by Atigun Pass to the oil fields on the Arctic Ocean. Gravel, calcium-chloride mud, trucks and almost no services: 245 miles with no fuel between Coldfoot and Deadhorse.","sources":[{"label":"Ray Jardine: 2025 Moto Alaska (July 2025)","url":"https://www.rayjardine.com/adventures/2025-07-Moto-Alaska/index.php"},{"label":"Freewheelings: how to survive the Dalton Highway by motorcycle","url":"https://www.freewheelings.com/how-to-survive-the-dalton-highway-haul-road-by-motorcycle/"}],"approximate":"Main stops on the Haul Road.","km":817,"bbox":[-150.8154,64.838,-147.5917,70.1999],"stops":[{"name":"Fairbanks","place":"Fairbanks, Alaska","at":[64.8378,-147.7167],"text":"Last big town: tyres, fuel cans, food.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Aerial_view_of_Fairbanks_Alaska_skyline_%28Quintin_Soloviev%29.jpg/500px-Aerial_view_of_Fairbanks_Alaska_skyline_%28Quintin_Soloviev%29.jpg","page":"Fairbanks, Alaska","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Fairbanks_Alaska_skyline_%28Quintin_Soloviev%29.jpg","credit":"Quintin Soloviev","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Livengood","place":"Livengood, Alaska","at":[65.5244,-148.5447],"text":"The start of the Dalton proper."},{"name":"Yukon River","place":"Yukon River Bridge","at":[65.8781,-149.7253],"text":"A wooden-decked bridge over the Yukon.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Patton_Yukon_River_Bridge.jpg/500px-Patton_Yukon_River_Bridge.jpg","page":"E. L. Patton Yukon River Bridge","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patton_Yukon_River_Bridge.jpg","credit":